From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: frontend combos from player 1's pad only (RelicOS)

In a game the frontend's own bits (input_driver_st.current_bits) are
gathered from every port, so the quit combo (Start+Select here) fires
from any pad, while hotkeys are read from player 1's port alone.
Observed on a handheld with a connected pad as player 1: Start+Select on
the handheld, player 2, left the game. Skip the other ports while a core
runs; in the menu every port still navigates when
input_all_users_control_menu says so.
---
diff -ruN a/input/input_driver.c b/input/input_driver.c
--- a/input/input_driver.c	2026-09-13 20:22:29.662026409 -0300
+++ b/input/input_driver.c	2026-09-13 20:22:29.680921870 -0300
@@ -6954,6 +6954,17 @@
             hotkey_port = 0;
       }
 
+#ifdef HAVE_MENU
+      /* RelicOS: in a game, only player 1's pad talks to the frontend --
+       * the quit and menu-toggle combos included, as the hotkeys already
+       * do; every other port is the core's alone. Observed on a handheld
+       * with a connected pad as player 1: Start+Select on player 2's pad
+       * left the game. In the menu every port navigates
+       * (input_all_users_control_menu), unchanged. */
+      if (!menu_is_alive && port != hotkey_port)
+         continue;
+#endif
+
       input_keys_pressed(
             port,
             hotkey_port,
